  "findings": [
    "A restoring the plane field during a successful merge does not remove the extra executed append-path work; it grows helper/all-region text and all-region frame.",
    "B retains flat before(...) and passes a local private three-field write_span to an ordinary inline helper, including A plane restoration. Every emitted function byte/relocation, constant and unwind payload is exact between A andB; source-qualified aggregate argument lowering adds no recovery on this actual TU.",
    "Both candidates preserve journal results in the independent O3 witness: source identity even for equal-valued distinct objects/types, exact plane, forward/reverse touching merge, disjoint spans both orderings and last-entry-only coalescing.",
    "No selection representation or physical consumer/kernel is changed. This rejects these two proposed lowerings; it does not prove all extra work is caused by flat records, nor that selection/alias/code-placement effects are absent.",
    "Both candidates are rejected; no live edit or native timing was performed. Residual AVX2 losses remain in native.json and native-cases.csv."
  ]
